<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Meet the Human-in-the-Loop team: five software engineering students building thoughtfully alongside AI.">
  <title>Team Human-in-the-Loop | Agentic SE Lab</title>
  <script>
    (() => {
      let theme;
      try {
        theme = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
      } catch (_) {}
      if (theme !== "light" && theme !== "dark") {
        theme = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light";
      }
      document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    :root {
      --accent: #E4007C;
      --bg: #FFF8E7;
      --text: #1D1D1F;
      --secondary: #5A5A5F;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --line: rgba(29, 29, 31, .13);
      --shadow: 0 1rem 2.5rem rgba(46, 36, 20, .07);
      color-scheme: light;
    }

    :root[data-theme="dark"] {
      --bg: #14142B;
      --text: #F4F1DE;
      --secondary: #B8B5A7;
      --card: #1F1F3D;
      --line: rgba(244, 241, 222, .15);
      --shadow: 0 1rem 2.5rem rgba(0, 0, 0, .18);
      color-scheme: dark;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      scroll-padding-top: 2rem;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      transition: background-color .2s ease, color .2s ease;
    }

    a { color: var(--accent); }
    a:focus-visible, button:focus-visible {
      outline: .18rem solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: .25rem;
    }

    .wrap {
      width: min(100% - 3rem, 70rem);
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .site-header {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .header-inner {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 2rem;
      padding-block: 2rem 4.5rem;
    }

    .brand {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .78rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: .16em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .brand span { color: var(--accent); }

    .header-copy { max-width: 47rem; }

    h1 {
      max-width: 12ch;
      margin: 2.4rem 0 1rem;
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6.4rem);
      font-weight: 760;
      letter-spacing: -.075em;
      line-height: .98;
    }

    .tagline {
      max-width: 38rem;
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    }

    .theme-toggle {
      display: inline-flex;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: .55rem;
      min-height: 2.8rem;
      padding: .55rem .9rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--card);
      color: var(--text);
      font: inherit;
      font-size: .92rem;
      font-weight: 650;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .theme-toggle:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
    .theme-icon { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1; }

    .header-mark {
      position: absolute;
      right: 8%;
      bottom: -3.8rem;
      width: 12rem;
      height: 12rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 50%;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .header-mark::before,
    .header-mark::after {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 1.2rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 50%;
      content: "";
    }

    .header-mark::after {
      inset: 2.4rem;
      border-color: var(--accent);
      opacity: .8;
    }

    main { padding-block: 4rem 5rem; }

    section + section { margin-top: 6rem; }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 .65rem;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: .78rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: .16em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .section-heading {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
      font-weight: 740;
      letter-spacing: -.055em;
      line-height: 1.08;
    }

    .section-intro {
      max-width: 43rem;
      margin: 1rem 0 2.5rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .member-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .member-card {
      display: flex;
      min-width: 0;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 1.25rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .member-avatar {
      display: block;
      width: 8rem;
      height: 8rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 50%;
      object-fit: cover;
      background: var(--bg);
    }

    .member-card h3 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      letter-spacing: -.035em;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .study {
      margin: .55rem 0 1rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .92rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .bio {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: .94rem;
    }

    .fun-fact {
      margin: .9rem 0 1.25rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .9rem;
    }

    .hot-take {
      margin: auto 0 0;
      padding: .65rem .8rem;
      border-radius: .65rem;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #fff;
      font-size: .84rem;
      font-weight: 650;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .future-panel {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 1.5rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .future-panel .section-intro { margin-bottom: 1.8rem; }

    .future-copy {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem;
    }

    .future-copy p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .future-note {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      padding-top: 1.2rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--text) !important;
      font-weight: 650;
    }

    footer {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--secondary);
      text-align: center;
      font-size: .85rem;
    }

    footer p { margin: 0; }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .wrap { width: calc(100% - 2rem); }
      .header-inner {
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1rem;
        padding-block: 1.25rem 3.5rem;
      }
      .header-copy { order: 1; }
      .theme-toggle { order: 0; align-self: flex-end; }
      h1 { margin-top: 1.8rem; }
      .member-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .future-copy { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .future-note { grid-column: auto; }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *, *::before, *::after {
        scroll-behavior: auto !important;
        transition-duration: .01ms !important;
        animation-duration: .01ms !important;
        animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="wrap header-inner">
      <div class="header-copy">
        <p class="brand"><span>UPB</span> · Agentic SE Lab</p>
        <h1>Human-in-the-Loop</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Five teammates, one big question: how do we build a future-proof future when the tools keep updating before the coffee cools?</p>
      </div>
      <button class="theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to night mode">
        <span class="theme-icon" aria-hidden="true">☾</span>
        <span class="theme-label">Night mode</span>
      </button>
      <div class="header-mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section id="team" aria-labelledby="team-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The people behind the prompts</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading" id="team-heading">Meet the team</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">A small crew exploring agentic software engineering—with humans still firmly in charge of the merge button. Profile details are intentionally left open where they weren’t supplied.</p>

      <div class="member-grid">
        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 160 160'%3E%3Crect width='160' height='160' rx='80' fill='%23DCEBE3'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='80' cy='62' r='29' fill='%23B97855'/%3E%3Cpath d='M49 61c2-29 17-42 33-42 25 0 39 19 34 47-11-4-22-16-27-24-11 13-23 19-40 19z' fill='%232A3540'/%3E%3Cpath d='M29 155c3-34 22-53 51-53s48 19 51 53' fill='%235E9180'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Avatar of Abu">
          <h3>Abu</h3>
          <p class="study">Study background not provided</p>
          <p class="bio">Abu is a member of the Human-in-the-Loop team. His study background, interests, fun fact, and personal view of AI were not included in the profile supplied for this page, so this introduction leaves those details open rather than inventing a biography. Abu can add what he enjoys building and what AI gets right—or spectacularly wrong—when he’s ready.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: not supplied yet.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Editorial placeholder—not submitted by Abu: an agent should bring tests, not just confidence.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 160 160'%3E%3Crect width='160' height='160' rx='80' fill='%23F3DFCC'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='80' cy='62' r='29' fill='%23D59A70'/%3E%3Cpath d='M49 59c0-27 14-40 32-40 23 0 37 16 35 43-17-3-29-12-37-24-7 12-18 18-30 21z' fill='%233E2E2A'/%3E%3Cpath d='M29 155c3-34 22-53 51-53s48 19 51 53' fill='%23CE8B63'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Avatar of Ayush">
          <h3>Ayush</h3>
          <p class="study">Study background not provided</p>
          <p class="bio">Ayush is part of the Human-in-the-Loop team. The profile provided for this page doesn’t include his study background, interests, fun fact, or current thoughts on AI in software engineering. Rather than give him a suspiciously polished fictional backstory, this card keeps the blanks visible. He can make it his own with a few details about what he likes to explore and build.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: not supplied yet.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Editorial placeholder—not submitted by Ayush: autocomplete is not the same thing as understanding.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 160 160'%3E%3Crect width='160' height='160' rx='80' fill='%23E9E2F2'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='80' cy='62' r='29' fill='%23A96849'/%3E%3Cpath d='M49 59c2-27 17-40 33-40 23 0 37 17 34 44-16-4-28-14-35-25-9 12-19 18-32 21z' fill='%232B2526'/%3E%3Cpath d='M29 155c3-34 22-53 51-53s48 19 51 53' fill='%237E6E9A'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Avatar of Bhavesh">
          <h3>Bhavesh</h3>
          <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, Paderborn University</p>
          <p class="bio">Bhavesh started an M.Sc. in Computer Science at Paderborn University in April 2026. He earned a B.E. in Computer Science from GH Raisoni Institute of Engineering and Business Management, Jalgaon, and completed a PG-Diploma in Advanced Computing at C-DAC. His stated interests include cricket, photography, and AI image generation. His fun fact and personal view of AI weren’t provided, so they’re left for him to fill in.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: not supplied yet.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Editorial placeholder—not submitted by Bhavesh: image generation is fun; attribution still matters.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 160 160'%3E%3Crect width='160' height='160' rx='80' fill='%23DDE6F1'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='80' cy='62' r='29' fill='%23C78661'/%3E%3Cpath d='M49 60c1-27 15-41 33-41 24 0 38 18 34 46-13-3-24-13-33-26-8 12-19 18-34 21z' fill='%23333843'/%3E%3Cpath d='M29 155c3-34 22-53 51-53s48 19 51 53' fill='%235E7899'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Avatar of Mahmud">
          <h3>Mahmud</h3>
          <p class="study">Study background not provided</p>
          <p class="bio">Mahmud is a member of the Human-in-the-Loop team. The profile available for this page doesn’t yet say what he studies, what he enjoys, or what he thinks about AI in software engineering today. So this introduction avoids the classic AI move of confidently filling in missing context. Mahmud can supply a study background, an interest, and a small fun fact to make it personal.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: not supplied yet.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Editorial placeholder—not submitted by Mahmud: the human review step is part of the feature.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 160 160'%3E%3Crect width='160' height='160' rx='80' fill='%23F1E8D5'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='80' cy='62' r='29' fill='%23B97B59'/%3E%3Cpath d='M49 59c2-28 17-40 33-40 24 0 38 18 34 46-15-3-27-13-34-25-9 12-19 18-33 19z' fill='%233B302B'/%3E%3Cpath d='M29 155c3-34 22-53 51-53s48 19 51 53' fill='%23B39156'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Avatar of Pruthvi">
          <h3>Pruthvi</h3>
          <p class="study">Study background not provided</p>
          <p class="bio">Pruthvi is part of the Human-in-the-Loop team. His supplied profile doesn’t include a study background, interests, fun fact, or personal perspective on AI-assisted software engineering. This card is deliberately a starting point, not a machine-generated life story. When Pruthvi adds a few details about what he cares about and what he’s learning, his introduction can grow beyond the strictly factual basics.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: not supplied yet.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Editorial placeholder—not submitted by Pruthvi: “it compiled” is a beginning, not a code review.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-heading">
      <div class="future-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our shared view</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" id="future-heading">The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">AI is changing how quickly we can turn an idea into a pull request. It hasn’t changed who should be accountable for what happens after.</p>
        <div class="future-copy">
          <p>We see AI as a capable collaborator: handy for exploring unfamiliar code, drafting the tedious first pass, and generating alternatives at 2 a.m. It can also produce a very convincing answer to the wrong question. Treat its output like a proposal, not a prophecy.</p>
          <p>In five to ten years, more routine implementation may be delegated to agents, while engineering work shifts toward describing goals, shaping systems, testing edge cases, and making careful trade-offs. The best teams will be the ones who know when to let the tools sprint—and when to ask them to explain themselves.</p>
          <p class="future-note">Our prediction: the future engineer’s most-used tool will be an agent. Their most important skill will still be judgment. Their most feared notification will remain “small merge conflict.”</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>Built by an agent, supervised by humans. · 2026 · Human-in-the-Loop</p>
  </footer>

  <script>
    (() => {
      const button = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");
      const icon = button.querySelector(".theme-icon");
      const label = button.querySelector(".theme-label");

      function updateButton(theme) {
        const night = theme === "dark";
        button.setAttribute("aria-label", night ? "Switch to day mode" : "Switch to night mode");
        icon.textContent = night ? "☀" : "☾";
        label.textContent = night ? "Day mode" : "Night mode";
      }

      updateButton(document.documentElement.dataset.theme);

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const next = document.documentElement.dataset.theme === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = next;
        updateButton(next);
        try {
          localStorage.setItem("upb-theme", next);
        } catch (_) {}
      });
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
